# Scripts run through an interpreter that reads the shebang and, for shell, the
# line endings themselves. A checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for
# Windows default) makes them CRLF, which Git Bash tolerates but Linux bash does
# not: from WSL or a container, scripts/boss fails with "$'\r': command not
# found", scripts/test/*.sh with "set: pipefail: invalid option name", and
# gradlew does not start. A trailing \r also breaks the node and python shebangs.
#
# Extension globs rather than scripts/**, which would also catch boss.bat and
# boss.ps1; the two extensionless scripts and gradlew are listed by name. Every
# mode-100755 file in the tree resolves to eol=lf through one of these, which the
# "Executable scripts are pinned to LF" CI step asserts.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
scripts/boss text eol=lf
scripts/publish-plugin text eol=lf
